  "title": "The Two-Weight Elevator",
  "family": "fiction",
  "category": "mechanical puzzles",
  "premise": "A puppet needs to lower a toy platform gently, but the two removable counterweight blocks together outweigh it and one alone underbalances it in the simplified model. The puppet transfers a small labeled trim block to the platform, brings the stated totals into balance, and uses a visible hand crank for controlled movement.",
  "hook": "The lift keeps choosing a side.",
  "visible_action": "Numbered weights hang from a visible cable; totals compare; trim block moves; crank rotates; platform descends one marked stop.",
  "intended_takeaway_or_theme": "A balance condition and a motion-control mechanism are separate questions.",
  "gate": "Define all masses and friction if used educationally; no numerical answer is asserted here. Not a real elevator, hoist, or suspended-load construction guide.",
